    "created_at": "2018-04-03T17:44:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-03T17:44:21Z",
    "body": "I fixed #3554 retroactively. Perhaps we should make the status check fail, instead of be pending, to prevent future such premature merges.\r\n\r\nThere's a slight chance that the next PR we land will be back to normal? But, this whole thing doesn't really make sense.\r\n\r\nMy current hypothesis is that this is some kind of GitHub bug, because the participation status checks should only ever be being posted to pull requests, and never to commits or to master. GitHub must somehow be trying to tie pull request status checks to master status checks, but doing a buggy job of it? Everything prior to March 10 has no participation status check (only a Travis CI status check), as I would expect. Whereas March 10 onward has a participation status check for the deleted PR #3547 somehow attached to it. For some reason.\r\n\r\nI'll email support.",
