    "created_at": "2018-04-26T18:08:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-26T18:08:20Z",
    "body": "GitHub support helpfully explained that this was due to the fact that the pull request was created between two branches of the repository, and then was deleted. The PR was then updated every time we pushed to master, causing us to mark all the commits on master with the status that was intended for the PR.\r\n\r\nThey've since fixed the problem by deleting the PR (delete in the GitHub UI just hides things).\r\n\r\nSince you cannot delete these bogus status checks (it's not allowed by the GitHub API), I'll instead overwrite them to indicate \"success\" and to point to this issue as an explanation.",
